-- The capacity refusals (S8 P3, Q-S8-3 (a), Q-S8-14 (a), Q-S8-15 (a)).
-- Each entry here makes a heap that grows with an entry argument: a fold
-- with the count n that allocates, or a list from an unfold with the limit
-- n. So `langc --kit build` refuses REFUSE_CAPACITY. `langc --kit eval`
-- still runs each entry. The modules that these defs come from keep a copy
-- with a literal count (examples/algebra.lang, test/ir/comb.lang,
-- test/ir/lazy.lang, test/ir/spine.lang, test/wasm/traps.lang).
def square : (n : Nat) -> Option Nat := fun (n : Nat) => fold (fun (acc : Option Nat) => bind acc (fun (a : Nat) => natAdd a n)) (some 0) n
